<title>UK: SocGen issues Eurobonds in francs and marks.</title>
<headline>SocGen issues Eurobonds in francs and marks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Societe Generale said it was lead managing for itself two subordinated six percent Eurobonds in French francs and marks.</p>
<p>The 10-year bonds are a 1.0 billion franc deal, to be priced 45 basis points over OATs, and a 300 million mark deal to be priced 53 b.p. over Bunds. </p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN FRF   COUPON     6.00	MATURITY    12.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    12.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+45 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    PAR/LUX   PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A+	  DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.50 PCT OCT.06 OAT / 5.50 PCT APR.07 OAT</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT    300 MLN DEM   COUPON     6.00	MATURITY    12.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    12.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.50	REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+53 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    PAR/LUX   PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A+	  DENOMS (K) 1	   SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.00 PCT BUND DUE JAN.07</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER.</p>
